CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among
hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the
freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs
and products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN OHL comes
in three variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal
licences: CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly
reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it,
in unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any
Licensor or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN
in the development of such designs.

1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-P.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

       a) any version of the CERN-OHL-P, or

       b) a licence which permits the Licensed Source to be used,
          copied, modified and distributed without restriction,
          including for commercial purposes.

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital
      code which can be applied to produce a Product.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available
      under this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object,
      whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use,
      application or processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Modified Source' means Covered Source to which modifications,
      additions, interfaces, patches, or other alterations have been
      made, the cumulative effect of which is that the Covered Source
      cannot be readily identified as the unmodified Covered Source.

  1.7 'You' means any individual or legal entity exercising rights
      under this Licence.

  1.8 'Licensor' means any person granting rights under this Licence.

  1.9 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,
      references to the location of any Notices, and all notices that
      refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties that
      are included in the Covered Source.

  1.10 'Licensee' means any person who receives Covered Source under
       this Licence.

2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, display,
      performance, and distribution of Covered Source. By exercising
      any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably accept
      these terms and conditions.

  2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and
      shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.

  2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the
      rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.

  2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing,
      or any other similar right.

3 Copying, Distributing and Modifying Covered Source

  3.1 You may copy and distribute verbatim copies of Covered Source,
      in any medium, provided You retain all Notices.

  3.2 You may modify Covered Source, other than Notices.

      You may only delete Notices if they are no longer applicable to
      the corresponding portion of the Covered Source (for example,
      a notice that is specific to a file that you have deleted).

      You may add your own copyright statement to modifications you
      have made to Covered Source, and may provide additional grant
      of rights by notifying recipients that they may use the
      modifications under terms of your choice, provided such terms
      do not restrict the rights of recipients under this Licence.

  3.3 You may distribute Covered Source with modifications complying
      with Section 3.2 provided that:

       a) you include a Notice to the recipient stating that you have
          modified the Covered Source; and

       b) the modified Covered Source carries prominent Notices
          stating that you have modified it, and giving a relevant
          date.

  3.4 You may distribute Products without restriction.

  3.5 You may use Covered Source to create Products and use, make,
      sell, offer for sale, import, and otherwise distribute such
      Products under terms of your choice, provided you do not
      restrict any recipient's rights in the Covered Source under
      this Licence.

4 Making and Distributing Products

  4.1 You may make Products, and/or convey them to recipients, under
      terms of your choice, provided that you:

       a) ensure that the Covered Source is available to those
          recipients under the terms of this Licence, and

       b) inform those recipients of the location(s) from which the
          Covered Source may be obtained.

  4.2 That information must be sufficient to allow them to obtain the
      Covered Source, and may be in the form of a URL, or a pointer to
      a location where the Covered Source is distributed.

5 Research and Non-Commercial Use

  This Licence does not restrict use of Covered Source for research
  and non-commercial purposes.

